-- Conclusion --
  Because the top corner of Box(d) is guaranteed present (any M from
  missing_lattice_points excludes polytope vertices by construction),
  the shift-polynomial diagonal entries -- and hence det(L) and the
  recovered threshold beta* -- are IDENTICAL for the box-minus-M
  support and the fully dense box. Deleting non-corner monomials from
  f changes neither dim(L) nor any individual diagonal entry, because
  the Jochemsz-May shift family is built from CONTAINMENT of f's
  support in Box(d), not from f's support being exactly Box(d).
  The leading asymptotic determinant exponent, and therefore the
  classical 1/2 threshold, survives UNCHANGED for this construction.

